<div class="global-demo">
  <p>
    Form 1, <span class="global-tag">global tag</span>: a
    <code>&lt;style global&gt;</code> rule. Any element with this class gets it.
  </p>
  <p>
    Form 2: select this sentence. The selection colour comes from an
    <code>@global</code> block.
  </p>
  <p class="frame">
    Form 3: <a href="/guide#style-global-rules">this link</a> is styled by an
    inline <code>:global(a)</code> inside a scoped selector.
  </p>
</div>

<style global>
  .global-tag {
    padding: 0 0.4rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    background: var(--accent);
    color: #fff;
  }
</style>

<style>
  .global-demo {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    color: var(--fg);

    p {
      margin: 0;
    }

    code {
      padding: 0 0.3rem;
      border-radius: 4px;
      background: var(--code);
      font-size: 0.9em;
    }

    .frame :global(a) {
      color: var(--accent);
      font-weight: 600;
    }
  }

  @global {
    ::selection {
      background: var(--accent);
      color: #fff;
    }
  }
</style>
